Package: forestPulse
Type: Package
Title: Analyse Forest Plots and Prepare Inputs for the 'iLand' Model
Version: 0.3.1
Authors@R: person(given = "Sushil", family = "Paudel", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "clarkesushil@gmail.com")
Description: Turns forest field sample plots and drone or satellite imagery
    into analysis-ready summaries, and assembles the input files needed by
    the 'iLand' forest landscape model. For field and image analysis, it
    summarises plot-level basal area, crown density and species composition,
    tidies species codes, locates trees from compass bearings and distances,
    indexes geotagged rasters into a searchable catalogue matched to plots,
    computes canopy height models and canopy-gap geometry, and derives
    red-green-blue vegetation indices. For model preparation, it imputes
    field plots to pixels to build wall-to-wall tree lists using modified
    random-forest imputation (Riley et al., 2016) <doi:10.1002/ecs2.1472>,
    derives daily climate variables such as vapour pressure deficit and
    radiation from 'gridMET' data (Abatzoglou, 2013) <doi:10.1002/joc.3413>
    following the FAO-56 approach (Allen et al., 1998, ISBN:9251042195), and
    builds stand grids, resource-unit environment files, tree-initialisation
    files and 'SQLite' climate databases for 'iLand'.
